l},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485181259,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDQ5OTcwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274499704"},"message":"Agree. Seems to be the most essential one for now. Looking into it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485184043,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDUxMjEyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274512122"},"message":"Note, that `git -c core.bare=False submodule add` works in direct mode in general. The issue is somehow more specific, which is good news, I think, since it doesn't look like we need a major design change.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485184485,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDUxNDI1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274514259"},"message":"I think I recall that some time back this approach also failed for some Git\nversions.\n\n\n\nOn Jan 23, 2017 16:07, \"Benjamin Poldrack\" \u003cnotifications@github.com\u003e wrote:\n\nNote, that git -c core.bare=False submodule add works in direct mode in\ngeneral. The issue is somehow more specific, which is good news, I think,\nsince it doesn't look like we need a major design change.\n\n—\nYou are receiving this because you authored the thread.\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003chttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274512122\u003e,\nor mute\nthe thread\n\u003chttps://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAIVH01X8TwtKXk_VZQEZLyxr8hZnAtDks5rVMIrgaJpZM4LrD_Z\u003e\n.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485184954,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDUxNjYwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274516601"},"message":"Just tried with git 1.7.9.5 - worked for me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485188421,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDUzNDY2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274534660"},"message":"Okay, this is weird. It happens within testrepo creation. But when I use the debugger to dig into it, I find a strange situation: The submodule to be added doesn't exist at all (not even the directory). Furthermore `git annex info` says the repo is in direct mode, while `ls` is showing a broken symlink.\n\nStill not sure, what this is about, but for now I don't think it's really the `git submodule add` what causes the trouble.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485189708,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDU0MTY3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274541676"},"message":"I can add the very same submodule to the very same annex repository in direct mode manually, while it fails with 'fatal: $program_name cannot be used without a working tree.' in the tests.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485264444,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDgwMjA4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274802083"},"message":"ATM using #1216 to figure it out.\n\nI guess I can fix the tests, but I don't know why yet.\nThis failure happens during testrepo creation, not within the actual tests. Those repositories are using `GitRepo._git_custom_command` for now in order to call git/git-annex. When I switch to a direct use of `Runner` it works. Couldn't reproduce it outside of the context of testrepo creation and I can't reproduce it within these repositories via shell either.\nWorth noting is another effect: Using `pdb.set_trace()` from within the testrepo's `populate()` method leads to nose just hanging. To get a debugger I can only raise a fake exception at that point and then running the test with `--pdb`. Don't know whether this is connected, but it's a strange thing and it occurs at the same time ...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485264541,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDgwMjQxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274802412"},"message":"@yarikoptic : Just in case the description above rings a bell - let me know.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1485279456,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDg3NzcxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274877719"},"message":"- `_git_custom_command` probably uses GitRunner, not just Runner so it might adjust environment etc -- verify that it is not the case\n- `leads to nose just hanging` -- probably there is a wrapping with `swallow_outputs` somewhere above it so all outputs are \"swallowed\" -- could remove/comment that context handler out for troubleshooting","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485294790,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDk1MDg4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274950883"},"message":"Re different environment: Right, I tried this but there's nothing indicating that this is causing the issue.\n\nRe `swallow_outputs`: Thanks. Will look for this.\n\n\n\nI think, I got it finally. @mih recalled correctly, there's something about using `-c core.bare=False`, that is troublesome with certain git version. While I tried an older git because of his hint, I missed checking a newer one. It's git version 2.11.0, that causes the issue. While using the shell as well as a \"pure\" `Runner` instance  are using my system-wide installation (2.7.0), we now use the bundled git delivered with git-annex-standalone when invoking via our Repo classes. And this is currently 2.11.0\n\nAs @mih pointed out in another issue, git 2.11.0 somehow ignores the per-call configuration passed via `-c core.bare=false`, while it still works if that value is set in `.git/config`.\n\nI'd consider this a bug in git, but probably we should talk to git folks. What do you think, @yarikoptic ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1485296074,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDk1NjU0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-274956548"},"message":"if it worked before -- indeed seems like a (regression) bug in git, what do you think @joeyh?  \nI would have quickly checked on #git IRC  showing a simple example on two version of git, and then took from there -- to either report to the mailing list or ...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485325844,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTAzMDE3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-275030174"},"message":"Independent of the Git version issue, can we make `care.bare=false` a permanent config setting while being in direct mode? Anything that would stop working if we did? I guess we would leave the repo in an unexpected state for non-annex-aware tools...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1485374215,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTIxNTUwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-275215506"},"message":"You are free to set core.bare=false in direct mode, but you lose a very\nimportant safeguard if you do this. It's quite easy to accidentially\ncommit large files into git, or run a git command that loses the content\nof annexed files when it's configured this way.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1485374305,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTIxNTkwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-275215907"},"message":"I'll bet the git developers won't see this as a regression. And to an\nextent rightly so. Direct mode's use of core.bare=true is surely a hack\n-- direct mode is entirely a hack -- and hacks break.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485402458,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTMwMTg1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-275301859"},"message":"For now I implemented a workaround, setting `core.bare=false` in `.git/config` in direct mode. But only on a per-call basis, so it is restored to original value after the git call. This slows down things a little bit, I guess, but until we come up with a better idea, it ensures things to work (not just `git submodule add`)\n\n@joeyh \n\n\u003e I'll bet the git developers won't see this as a regression. And to an\nextent rightly so. Direct mode's use of core.bare=true is surely a hack\n-- direct mode is entirely a hack -- and hacks break.\n\nWell, what I consider a bug here actually isn't about `core.bare` from my point of view. Instead `-c` option is supposed to overrule whatever `.git/config` says, so ignoring this setting is a break of `git`'s API, isn't it?","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485402496,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDkzNzI1Mzg2OQ=="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1485874950,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NjM4NjkyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1208#issuecomment-276386925"},"message":"Benjamin Poldrack wrote:\n\u003e Well, what I consider a bug here actually isn't about core.bare from my point\n\u003e of view. Instead -c option is supposed to overrule whatever .git/config says,\n\u003e so ignoring this setting is a break of git's API, isn't it?\n\nAs yes, that sounds like a bug indeed.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486664432,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTU2MDYyMjAy"},"status":2}]}